================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

The desktop application distributes third-party software in binary form. This
is redistribution, not mere use, so each component's license terms apply to the
distributed artifacts.

The inventory below is INCOMPLETE: it records what is redistributed, but the
license of each dependency has not yet been verified one by one. Complete it
before publishing signed releases:

    pip install pip-licenses && pip-licenses --format=markdown --with-urls
    npm --prefix desktop ls --all --json
    npm --prefix dashboard/frontend ls --all --json

Pay particular attention to any GPL/AGPL-licensed transitive dependency, since
the desktop application ships its dependency tree rather than merely using it.

Redistributed in the packaged installers:

  * Electron, including its bundled Chromium and Node.js runtimes
  * The Python dependency tree frozen into the backend sidecar by PyInstaller
      -> roots are declared in agentic-cli/pyproject.toml and dashboard/backend
  * PyInstaller bootloader code embedded in the frozen binary
      -> PyInstaller's license carries an exception governing the terms under
         which frozen applications may be distributed; confirm its current
         wording covers this project's distribution model

NOT redistributed (referenced or fetched at runtime, absent from the installer):

  * Neo4j - referenced via docker-compose; the user supplies the server
  * The optional built-in language model - downloaded on first use into
    ~/.keel/models at the user's request; nothing ships in the installer

Where a dependency's own license requires attribution, reproduce its NOTICE
content here.
